  "news": [
    {
      "date": "Wed, Sep 23, 2026",
      "iso": "2026-09-23",
      "tag": "",
      "title": "Sept 23rd (Week3)",
      "body": "A GOALTENDING BATTLE FOR THE AGES\nIf you were one of the lucky fans holding a ticket for last night’s matchup in Châteauguay, consider yourself privileged — you witnessed one hell of a battle between the pipes.\nReplacement goalie Eric “Superman” faced an incredible 48 shots, making some absolutely spectacular saves. \nHe saved some of his best work for the final six minutes, including an absolute robbery on Shane, who looked certain to bury a beauty upstairs. Superman had other plans and left Shane shaking his head — and empty-handed.\n\nMARTINEZ IS BACK!\nAfter taking nearly three months away from the rink, Martinez returned with one of his best performances ever, lighting the lamp THREE TIMES!\nThat’s right — HAT TRICK!\nRumour has it there were so many hats thrown onto the ice that officials needed 10 minutes to clean them all up. Châteauguay hasn’t seen that much headwear since the last clearance sale at Lids.\n\nJ WHITE STANDS TALL\nAt the other end, J White was pushing his limits with some outstanding stretch saves, doing everything possible to keep the Levesque brothers from padding their point totals.\nWhite reportedly suffered a slight groin injury, but early reports indicate he’ll survive. Sources close to the team say the man has balls of steel, so apparently there’s not much concern in that department. 😂\n\nTSN IS BACK\nTSN was on-site again this week for exclusive pre- and post-game interviews.\nAll video links will be posted over the next few days, including player reactions and some hard-hitting journalism from inside the CAHL locker room.\n\nHEALTHY SCRATCH REPORT\nA few familiar names were missing from the lineup last night, including Goodleaf, Howell and Blenman — players who normally bring the energy level up another notch.\nBut despite missing some firepower, the boys did just fine without them.\nAnother Wednesday night in the books.\n\nBig saves. Big goals. A hat trick. Balls of steel.\nJust another night in the CAHL. 🏒🔥\n\nBelow are the game details, \nGame 1 – Black 5, White 1\nGame 2 – Black 3, White 5\nGame 3 – Black 3, White 2\n\nThe 3 stars of the game were , \n1.        Danny Martinez\n2.        JF Fournier\n3.        Shane Ford",
      "pinned": false
    },
    {
      "date": "Wed, Sep 16, 2026",
      "iso": "2026-09-16",
      "tag": "",
      "title": "Sept 16th (Week2)",
      "body": "3 year contract for Carter Howell with 87 points in his last season with the hounddogs-\nChateauguay - The  CAHL league is happy to announce a 3 year deal signed in August with youngblood Carter Howell who accepted the offer to join the league during the offseason. \nHowell set a record in his first 3 seasons with his former HoundDogs team as the top goal scorer in the league finishing each season with 87 plus points. He will be a great addition to the gang. He was interviewed this week in the bathroom of the golf course while taking a dump in prep for his annual tournament and said he was really looking forward to joining to contribute to the fun of the Chateauguay league.",
      "pinned": false
    },
    {
      "date": "Wed, Sep 9, 2026",
      "iso": "2026-09-09",
      "tag": "",
      "title": "Sept 9th (Week1)",
      "body": "3 year contract for Aruntase Paul with 55 points in his last season with the Icestingers-\nChateauguay - The  CAHL league is also pleased to announce another 3 year deal signed in August with Paul who accepted the offer to join the league during the offseason. \nPaul is a 6ft 2 roadrunner who breaks energy to the ice every game with eyes in the back if his head.  In his last season with the IceDogs, Paul locked in 98 points and as the top defensemen drafted, he will be another great addition to the league. In his interview earlier this week, Paul noted that playing with the old guys is so much more fun.",
      "pinned": false
    },
    {
      "date": "Thu, Sep 3, 2026",
      "iso": "2026-09-03",
      "tag": "",
      "title": "Welcome to the 2026–2027 Season!",
      "body": "Hi everyone,\nGreat start to the winter season. The white team comeback was outstanding in week1.  As we all discussed many times, its not really cool to keep the game going after a two goal lead after hitting 5 goals as it can get out of hand but last night was an exception. The ideal way to play all games is by resetting the score back to 0 once the score hits 5 and there is a two-goal difference. I know some of you don't like that, but with spares and team balancing, its the best way. \n\nCollections -\nA few things I want to remind everyone. If you have played one game then you should have made a payment towards your registration fees. If that's not the case, please send me an Etransfer. I feel like a bill collector, the worst part of my job is trying to collect money.\n\nTime on the ice -\nThe other thing, is time on the ice per shift. Be conscious of the clock when your on the ice, try hard not to stay of the ice for 5 minutes as the next line will get cold and will get angry and do the same thing. Be fair which will result in more icetime all around.\n\nThe Referee -\nThe last thing we all want to hear are complaints on the ice that Nick missed a call or and offside or didn't see a slashing call or whatever. Please refrain from giving nick comments. This is garage hockey and the ultimate goal is to have fun, a few good laughs and of course a few cold beers or Gatorade after the game.",
      "pinned": false
    }
  ]
}
